Write a Python module that transcribes a short patient audio recording into
Spanish text using the ElevenLabs Speech-to-Text API.

Interface:

    transcribe(audio_path: str, language_code: str = "es") -> Transcript

    Transcript is a dataclass with:
        text: str
        language_code: str
        duration_s: float

Implementation: use the official elevenlabs Python SDK. Read
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY from the environment; raise a clear error at import time
if absent.

Call client.speech_to_text.convert(file=..., model_id="scribe_v1",
language_code=...). Do not assume more of the response schema than
`.text` and `.language_code`; guard against a missing or empty transcript.

Raise SttError on API failure, timeout (15 second cap), or an empty
transcript, with a message naming the stage as "listen".

This module is the "ears" half of voice_agent — see tts_python.prompt for
the "mouth" half and pipeline_python.prompt for how a turn's transcript
feeds into the structured intake.
